(An assertion between two readings of one value, as one renderable line:
 `If <a> is not <b> then, Print "ASSERT ROW: expected {b} got {a}", Exit
 95. Print <a>` - the internal period closes the If, the trailing Print
 takes whatever punctuation 'gen join lines' adds (the same shape as
 gen_buffers.vox's 'gen assert number', which this reuses).)

(ENV-02, ENV-05: `count` is the number of variables (LANGUAGE.md:4479)
 and `empty` is true iff there are none (4482) - so count is 0 exactly
 when empty is true, whatever the host's environment holds. Each property
 is read into a named variable or used inline, at random, and the two
 directions of the agreement are two lines in either order.)

To 'gen leaf environment agreement' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_envs to gen_envs add 1.
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a text called 'the count' is "environment's count".
    a number called 'the count draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the count draw' is 0 then,
        a text called 'the count stem' is 'gen environment name',
        Set 'the count' to 'gen buffer reference' of 'the count stem',
        append "a number called {'the count'} is environment's count" to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the emptiness' is "environment's empty".
    a number called 'the emptiness draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the emptiness draw' is 0 then,
        a text called 'the emptiness stem' is 'gen environment name',
        Set 'the emptiness' to 'gen buffer reference' of 'the emptiness stem',
        append "a boolean called {'the emptiness'} is environment's empty" to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the emptiness shown' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the emptiness'.
    a text called 'the count shown' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the count'.
    a text called 'none but not empty' is "If {'the count'} is 0 and {'the emptiness'} is false then, Print \"ASSERT ENV-02: expected 1 got {'the emptiness shown'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the emptiness'}".
    a text called 'some but empty' is "If {'the count'} is not 0 and {'the emptiness'} then, Print \"ASSERT ENV-05: expected 0 got {'the emptiness shown'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the count'} as a boolean".
    a number called 'the order draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the order draw' is 0 then,
        append 'none but not empty' to 'the lines',
        append 'some but empty' to 'the lines'.
    If 'the order draw' is 1 then,
        append 'some but empty' to 'the lines',
        append 'none but not empty' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(ENV-06 (ENV-07, ENV-09 folded), ENV-03, ENV-04: a text-valued property -
 the named lookup, `first`, or `last` - read into a `text` the manual's
 own way (LANGUAGE.md:4485-4494), and then again into whichever of the
 other receivers the manual allows for a text value: a `buffer` declared
 straight from the property, a second such buffer, a `value`. The text is
 copied into a buffer of its own so it can be measured, and every pair of
 readings is asserted to agree - same `size`, same `empty`, and a `value`
 is equal to the text. How many extra readings, which kinds, and their
 order are drawn. When the name is one the generator invented, `exists`
 on it is asserted false as well (ENV-10).)

To 'gen leaf environment lookup' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_envs to gen_envs add 1.
    a text called 'the source' is 'gen environment source'.
    a text called 'the row' is gen_environment_last_row.
    a boolean called 'the name is unset' is gen_environment_last_name_is_unset.
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a text called 'the text stem' is 'gen environment name'.
    a text called 'the text' is 'gen buffer reference' of 'the text stem'.
    append "a text called {'the text'} is {'the source'}" to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the measure' is 'gen environment companion' of "in bytes".
    a text called 'the measure size' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the measure' and "size".
    a text called 'the measure emptiness' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the measure' and "empty".
    append "a buffer called {'the measure'} is {'the text'}" to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the closing read' is "Print {'the measure size'}".
    (One to three further readings, each a receiver the manual allows
     for a text value, each asserted against the measuring copy.)
    a number called 'the extra readings' is 'rng below' of 3 add 1.
    a number called 'the reading' is 0.
    While 'the reading' is less than 'the extra readings',
        a number called 'the receiver draw' is 'rng below' of 3,
        a text called 'the stem' is 'gen environment name',
        a text called 'the name' is 'gen buffer reference' of 'the stem',
        If 'the receiver draw' is less than 2 then,
            a text called 'the direct size' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the stem' and "size",
            a text called 'the direct emptiness' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the stem' and "empty",
            append "a buffer called {'the name'} is {'the source'}" to 'the lines',
            a text called 'the size agreement' is 'gen assert number matches' of 'the row' and 'the direct size' and 'the measure size',
            append 'the size agreement' to 'the lines',
            a text called 'the emptiness shown' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the measure emptiness',
            a text called 'the direct shown' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the direct emptiness',
            append "If {'the direct emptiness'} is not {'the measure emptiness'} then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected {'the emptiness shown'} got {'the direct shown'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the direct emptiness'}" to 'the lines',
            Set 'the closing read' to "Print {'the direct size'}".
        If 'the receiver draw' is 2 then,
            append "a value called {'the name'} is {'the source'}" to 'the lines',
            append "If {'the name'} is not {'the text'} then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected the text got a different value\", Exit 95. Print {'the measure emptiness'}" to 'the lines'.
        Set 'the reading' to 'the reading' add 1.
    If 'the name is unset' then,
        a text called 'the unset name' is 'gen environment variable name unset from' of 'the source',
        append "If the environment variable \"{'the unset name'}\" exists then, Print \"ASSERT ENV-10: expected 0 got 1\", Exit 95. Print {'the measure emptiness'}" to 'the lines'.
    append 'the closing read' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(The bare variable name back out of a source expression the lookup leaf
 built - `environment's "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_123"` gives VOXFUZZ_UNSET_123.
 Byte arithmetic on a text the generator wrote itself a moment ago.)

To 'gen environment variable name unset from' with a text called 'the source'.
    a buffer called 'the source bytes' is "{'the source'}".
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the source bytes's size.
    a text called 'the name so far' is "".
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    a boolean called 'inside the quotes' is false.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the byte here' is byte 'the position' of 'the source bytes',
        (Three flat Ifs, not one nested pair: a nested If closed by a
         single period leaves its parent open, and the increment below
         would fall inside it - the loop then never advances. Found by
         this very function hanging the unit test.)
        If 'the byte here' is 34 and 'inside the quotes' then,
            Set 'the position' to 'the byte count'.
        If 'the byte here' is 34 and 'inside the quotes' is false then,
            Set 'inside the quotes' to true.
        If 'the byte here' is not 34 and 'inside the quotes' then,
            a buffer called 'the one byte' is 1 bytes in size,
            Set byte 1 of 'the one byte' to 'the byte here',
            Set 'the name so far' to "{'the name so far'}{'the one byte'}".
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    Return a text, 'the name so far'.

(ENV-10, ENV-11: `If the environment variable "NAME" exists then,` is a
 predicate (LANGUAGE.md:4512-4517). Two readings of it on one name must
 agree; on a name the generator invented it must be false. Each line
 keeps its If closed and ends on a plain statement, and the manual's
 Otherwise branch and its Complete Example's `If ... But if ... exists`
 fallback (4519-4540) are each emitted sometimes - the fallback with an
 invented name, so what the program prints is the flag value the harness
 passed and never a host value.)

To 'gen leaf environment exists' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_envs to gen_envs add 1.
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a text called 'the variable' is 'gen environment variable name'.
